# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD boots the BACnet/IP simulator on UDP 0.0.0.0:47808 (no
# firewall) then execs `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * the vulnerable service is ALREADY LISTENING on all interfaces when the
#     agent starts (a do-nothing agent must fail the firewall check);
#   * PID 1 is `sleep infinity`, so nothing a solution does can kill the box.
#
# The remediation is a network-layer compensating control (iptables), applied
# LIVE to the running kernel table - there is no daemon-restart step, so there
# is no "edited config but forgot to restart" case for this scenario.
